{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Deploy job runs on non-production branch",
    "Explanation": [
      "The pipeline is green because all three jobs succeeded, but this does not meet the requirement. The commit was on branch 'koans-08-branch-filters', not 'production', and the deploy job still ran. The config has no branch filter on deploy, so it is eligible on every branch. Its 'requires: [test-production]' only orders deploy after test-production, and that job also runs on any branch. The fix belongs in the workflow's job entry for deploy, not in the job definition, because CircleCI branch filters are declared under workflows. Adding 'filters: branches: only: production' makes production the only branch deploy can run on. 'ignore' would be an allow-by-default denylist that new branches could slip past."
