{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Beta tag filters needed on all workflow jobs",
    "Explanation": [
      "The frozen workflow.txt shows pipeline #156 with workflow build-test-and-deploy SUCCESS and all three jobs (build, test, deploy) SUCCESS, so the pipeline is green. However, the frozen config.yml defines no `filters` on any job. In CircleCI, jobs without tag filters never run for tag pushes, so the required beta-tagged release flow would not execute at all; and on branch/API triggers (as seen here, trigger: API on branch koans-09-tag-filters) deploy runs unconditionally, violating the rule that only beta-pattern tags should trigger deployment and non-beta tags must not. Hence the behaviour is not correct. Because deploy requires test, which requires build, CircleCI demands that every upstream job in a tag-triggered chain also carry matching tag filters; otherwise deploy would never run on the tag. Therefore the fix must add `filters: tags: only: \u003cbeta pattern\u003e` (with branches ignored as appropriate) to all jobs in the workflow (build, test, and deploy), not just deploy, so the full chain participates in the beta-tagged flow while non-beta tags are excluded."
    ],
